    "body": "Fix v0.2.0's binary reporting \"HoneyBee Browser v0.1.0\" on startup. The version is defined in four places -- the CONTRIBUTING gotcha documented only two.\n\n## The bug\n\n    $ ./build/bin/honeybee\n    HoneyBee Browser v0.1.0        <- on a v0.2.0 binary\n\nFour places hold the version:\n\n1. CMakeLists.txt (VERSION -- informational)\n2. src/base/version.cpp (version_string -- source of truth)\n3. tests/test_version.cpp (hardcoded assertions)\n4. src/main.cpp (startup banner -- was a hardcoded literal)\n\n## What changed\n\nVersion bumped 0.1.0 -> 0.2.1 in CMakeLists.txt, version.cpp, and test_version.cpp.\n\nsrc/main.cpp now calls honeybee::version_string() instead of hardcoding the banner. This removes the drift risk rather than moving the hardcoded value to a new number.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md gotcha #4 updated: two places -> three places, plus a note that the banner now auto-updates.\n\nversion.hpp doc comment updated for consistency.\n\n## The tests caught it\n\nAfter bumping version.cpp, test_version.cpp failed with:\n\n    REQUIRE(honeybee::version_string() == \"0.1.0\")\n      with expansion: \"0.2.1\" == \"0.1.0\"\n\nThe tests were doing exactly their job. That is why test_version.cpp is the third source of truth: it fails loudly if you forget it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Build: recompiles version.cpp and main.cpp, relinks bin/honeybee\n- Tests: 165 cases, 669 assertions, all pass\n- Banner after this PR: HoneyBee Browser v0.2.1 (confirmed with stdbuf)\n\n## Plan after merge\n\n1. Tag v0.2.1 on the merge commit\n2. Push tag to both remotes\n3. Publish GitHub release for v0.2.1 (patch; notes explain the drift)\n4. v0.2.0 tag stays in history -- no force-push\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-20T11:51:35Z",
